**Solution**

Use the ideal‑gas equation  

\[
PV=nRT
\]

where  

* \(P\) = pressure at the lunar surface  
* \(V\) = volume we want  
* \(n\) = amount of gas (mol)  
* \(R = 0.082057\ \text{L·atm·K}^{-1}\text{·mol}^{-1}\)  
* \(T = 100\ \text{K}\).

---

### 1.  Pressure in atm  

The given pressure is \(P = 10^{-10}\ \text{torr}\).

\[
1\ \text{atm}=760\ \text{torr}\;\Longrightarrow\;
P = \frac{10^{-10}}{760}\ \text{atm}
      = 1.315789\times10^{-13}\ \text{atm}
\]

---

### 2.  (a)  \(10^{6}\) molecules  

Number of moles  

\[
n = \frac{10^{6}}{N_{\!A}}
    = \frac{10^{6}}{6.022\times10^{23}}
    = 1.6605\times10^{-18}\ \text{mol}
\]

Insert in \(PV=nRT\):

\[
V = \frac{nRT}{P}
   = \frac{(1.6605\times10^{-18}\,\text{mol})(0.082057\ \text{L·atm·K}^{-1}\text{·mol}^{-1})(100\ \text{K})}
          {1.315789\times10^{-13}\ \text{atm}}
\]

\[
V = \frac{1.362\times10^{-17}\ \text{L·atm}}{1.315789\times10^{-13}\ \text{atm}}
   = 1.04\times10^{-4}\ \text{L}
\]

---

### 3.  (b)  1 mmol  

\(n = 1\ \text{mmol} = 10^{-3}\ \text{mol}\)

\[
V = \frac{(10^{-3}\,\text{mol})(0.082057\ \text{L·atm·K}^{-1}\text{·mol}^{-1})(100\ \text{K})}
          {1.315789\times10^{-13}\ \text{atm}}
   = \frac{8.2057\times10^{-3}\ \text{L·atm}}{1.315789\times10^{-13}\ \text{atm}}
   = 6.24\times10^{10}\ \text{L}
\]

---

### 4.  Result  

\[
\boxed{\text{(a)}\;1.04\times10^{-4}\ \text{L}\qquad 
       \text{(b)}\;6.24\times10^{10}\ \text{L}}
\]

These numbers correspond to **option E** in the list.

Le prix de vente est obtenu en appliquant la majoration de 40 % au coût d’achat :

\[
\text{Prix de vente}= \text{Coût} \times (1+0{,}40)
                 = 18{,}75 \times 1{,}40
                 = 18{,}75 \times \frac{14}{10}
                 = \frac{18{,}75 \times 14}{10}
                 = \frac{262{,}5}{10}
                 = 26{,}25\text{ $}
\]

Donc la bonne réponse est **G) 26,25 $**.
